    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The Andromeda Strain (1971) revolutionized scientific accuracy in sci-fi thrillers. Director Robert Wise meticulously adapts Michael Crichton's novel with documentary-like precision, establishing a template for \"hard sci-fi\" that influenced films like <a href=\"/movie/6950\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"6950\">Outbreak</a> (1995) and <a href=\"/movie/39538\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"39538\">Contagion</a> (2011). The film's clinical approach - showing scientists methodically working through containment protocols and research procedures - created a new standard for realistic science fiction that stands in stark contrast to the B-movie creature features of its era."
      },
      {
        "type": "movies",
