      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's innovative split-screen techniques and computer readout displays were revolutionary for 1971, predating similar visual approaches in films like <a href=\"/movie/891\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"891\">All the President's Men</a> (1976) and <a href=\"/movie/592\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"592\">The Conversation</a> (1974). The sterile, modernist set design of Project Wildfire's underground lab influenced countless scientific facility depictions, from <a href=\"/movie/348\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"348\">Alien</a> (1979) to <a href=\"/movie/264660\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"264660\">Ex Machina</a> (2014)."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "What sets The Andromeda Strain apart is its commitment to process over spectacle. Unlike later virus thrillers like 12 Monkeys (1995) or <a href=\"/movie/170\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"170\">28 Days Later</a> (2002), the film treats its scientists as methodical problem-solvers rather than action heroes. The deliberate pacing and attention to scientific detail created a new subgenre of procedural sci-fi that continues with films like <a href=\"/movie/329865\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"329865\">Arrival</a> (2016). SUBHEAD: Legacy and Influence"
      },
      {
        "type": "movies",
        "movies": [
          {
            "title": "Arrival",
            "year": 2016,
            "slug": "Linguist Louise Banks leads a scientific team attempting to communicate with mysterious aliens. Emphasizes scientific methodology.",
            "poster": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/x2FJsf1ElAgr63Y3PNPtJrcmpoe.jpg",
            "initialStreaming": "Hulu",
            "tmdb_id": 329865,
            "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/x2FJsf1ElAgr63Y3PNPtJrcmpoe.jpg"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's influence extends beyond science fiction. Its documentary-style approach to crisis management inspired disaster films like <a href=\"/movie/988\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"988\">The China Syndrome</a> (1979) and <a href=\"/movie/568\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"568\">Apollo 13</a> (1995). The concept of an underground government facility dealing with extraterrestrial threats became a template for everything from <a href=\"/movie/840\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"840\">Close Encounters of the Third Kind</a> (1977) to <a href=\"/movie/1091\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1091\">The Thing</a> (1982)."
      }
